pyramid Information Governance Model for a Regional Health Network

// stress: long-labels — tier names of 50–70 characters with descriptions of 80–100 characters

Board-approved enterprise policy on clinical data stewardship and patient consent
  The board reviews the policy every year and signs off on any change to patient data sharing agreements.

Domain data owners accountable for quality and lawful use within each service line
  Each owner publishes a quarterly attestation covering completeness, timeliness and access exceptions.

Cross-organisation data standards and shared reference code sets for interoperability
  A standards group maintains the common vocabularies used by hospitals, clinics and community providers.

Local stewardship teams embedded in hospitals, clinics and community care programmes
  Stewards resolve duplicate patient records and escalate unresolved identity conflicts within two days.

Day-to-day data entry practice by frontline clinical and administrative staff
  Staff complete annual training and follow the point-of-entry checklists for every new registration.
